  "summary_en": "This is the ULSE store page for ANSI/CAN/UL 3100, the safety standard for battery-operated automated mobile platforms. These are used indoors, or outdoors in commercial or industrial settings, to lift, carry, pick and tow loads. The page lists the scope, the exclusions (industrial robots, floor-cleaning machines, forklifts, and transporting people) and the 2026 revisions to electrical, impact and vibration tests.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Covers battery-powered (lead acid or lithium) automated mobile platforms with or without payload for lifting, carrying, picking, towing",
   "Excludes industrial robots (UL 1740/CSA Z434), though compliant manipulators may be payloads",
   "Excludes forklifts/industrial trucks and floor cleaning machines, and person transport",
   "Off-board chargers to be installed per NEC and Canadian Electrical Code",
   "2026 revision redefines hazardous voltage as 60 VDC and modifies impact and vibration tests"
  ],
